{"id":790,"slug":"the-leopard","title":"The Leopard","year":1963,"country":"Italy","duration":185,"spine":235,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/790-the-leopard","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/96833308352eedd79b50b2de8016a6c5/7IQOqWTrRuJg90rWrJZbK1VXI7aDcR_large.jpg","description":"Making its long-awaited U.S. home video debut, Luchino Visconti’s The Leopard (Il Gattopardo) is an epic on the grandest possible scale. The film recreates, with nostalgia, drama, and opulence, the tumultuous years of Italy's Risorgimento—when the aristocracy lost its grip and the middle classes rose and formed a unified, democratic Italy. Burt Lancaster stars as the aging prince watching his culture and fortune wane in the face of a new generation, represented by his upstart nephew (Alain Delon) and his beautiful fiancée (Claudia Cardinale). Awarded the Palme d’Or at the 1963 Cannes Film Festival, The Leopard translates Giuseppe Tomasi di Lampedusa's novel, and the history it recounts, into a truly cinematic masterpiece. The Criterion Collection is proud to present the film in two distinct versions: Visconti’s original Italian version, and the alternate English-language version released in America in a newly restored special edition.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Luchino Visconti","slug":"luchino-visconti"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Burt Lancaster","role":"Don Fabrizio Corbera, Prince of Salina","slug":"burt-lancaster"},{"actor":"Claudia Cardinale","role":"Angelica Sedàra","slug":"claudia-cardinale"},{"actor":"Alain Delon","role":"Tancredi Falconeri","slug":"alain-delon"},{"actor":"Paolo Stoppa","role":"Don Calógero Sedàra","slug":"paolo-stoppa"},{"actor":"Rina Morelli","role":"Maria Stella Corbera, Princess of Salina","slug":"rina-morelli"},{"actor":"Romolo Valli","role":"Father Pirrone","slug":"romolo-valli"},{"actor":"Mario Girotti","role":"Count Cavriaghi","slug":"mario-girotti"},{"actor":"Pierre Clémenti","role":"Francesco Paolo Corbera","s